# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **File**: `package.json` and `package-lock.json`
- **Action**: Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- **Version**: Added as a new dependency (managed by npm)

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
- **File**: `app/layout.tsx`
- **Actions**:
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout inside the `<body>` tag, after the children
- **Rationale**: This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects, ensuring seamless integration with Next.js routing

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide:
1. Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. Identified this as a Next.js App Router project (Next.js 14.2.35)
3. Applied framework-specific instructions for App Router layout integration
4. Placed the Analytics component at the end of the body tag as recommended

## Verification Completed

✅ **Build**: Project builds successfully without errors
✅ **Linting**: ESLint passes with no warnings or errors
✅ **Tests**: No test script configured (skipped as expected)
✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file updated correctly

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics → Enable)
3. Analytics will automatically start collecting data after deployment

## Files Modified

- `tgs-ui/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `tgs-ui/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `tgs-ui/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

All changes preserve the existing code structure and only add the necessary Analytics integration.
